  "description": "config.yaml's knob sections (Storage §2.5, session model §11, terminal-size §3, grid-snapshot rule 12): the sections the contract fixes, key for key, with each range as the loader enforces it. Valid: the knob sections of the lab config template with synthetic values, every required knob present, the two inventory knobs included. Invalid: a missing required knob; an out-of-range timers.keepalive_count_max. The cross-key rule keepalive_probe_interval below keepalive_interval is prose (R4): the instance that breaks it is listed as the loader's refusal case, and only U5's loader test grades it. The top level is open: listen_addr, the paths, credentials and capture are deployment-local, not contract. A bare 0 is also a Go duration (the loader's time.ParseDuration accepts it): keepalive_interval 0 and 0s both validate, while a unit-less 5 is not a duration.",
  "corpus": [
    "Storage §2.1",
    "Storage §2.5",
    "Storage §7.3",
    "session model §11",
    "terminal-size §3",
    "grid-snapshot rule 12"
  ],
